          "id": "SP_PNEUMODERMA_MEDITERRANEUM_VAN_BENEDEN_1838",
          "name": "Pneumoderma mediterraneum Van Beneden, 1838",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Pneumoderma",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p>External description: <em>Allapasus isidis </em>is light yellow in body color, although in the region of the hepatic intestine, the dark brown gut can be seen. The overall body shape is more compacted (less than half of the length-to-width ratio) in <em>A. isidis </em>than in <em>A. aurantiacus </em>(Holland et al. 2012). Edges of the lateral wings were in contact with each other along the trunk in the observed captured holotype, but spread apart when observed by the ROV. [Priede, 2012]</p><p>Internal description: Internal anatomy is very similar to that already described for <em>A. aurantiacus </em>[Holland et al. 2012], therefore only features of special interest will be described here. The stomochord is packed with a mass of cells with vacuoles but no lumen. In the collar, a small proboscis skeleton separates the stomochord from the main digestive tract. One side of the pharyngeal region of the trunk is characterized by gill pores running in a row on either side of the nerve cord. Hundreds of testes run lateral to the gill pores, and are visible through the top epidermis. Each testis comprises a peripheral zone of immature spermatogenic cells and a central lumen filled with mature sperm. The intestines (prehapatic, hepatic, and posthepatic regions) resemble the intestinal regions in <em>A. aurantiacus.</em><em> </em>The only known specimen of <em>A. isidis</em> is the male holotype.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:2305834",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "ad025d94-3506-5a3-a16-61e118b962e0f2",
          "sourceIds": {
            "itis": [
              "78070"
            ],
            "col": [
              "4KKVW"
            ]
          },
          "authorityIds": "col:4KKVW,itis:78070"
